{
  "about": "Solana nodes as templates the vault enforces (solguard::template, contracts/vault/src/soltemplates.rs): every instruction is checked byte by byte before the vault signs. Accounts: 'vault' is the vault itself, 'vault_ata' its own token account for the mint at position mint_at (re-derived, so proceeds can't go anywhere else), 'new_signer' a fresh key (a new LP position), 'fixed' a pinned address, 'any' an account the program itself checks against the others (pool PDAs, bin arrays). Trailing extra accounts are never signers. needs_owner: the owner's own Solana wallet must co-sign (set with sol_owner_wallet). Values in {braces} are set per coin by the owner and filled in when the template is saved. Tested on a Solana mainnet fork (surfpool): contracts/sandbox/tests/sol_fork.rs, sol_fork_meteora.rs.",
